---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const steps = [
  { n: "01", t: "Shade",    s: ["Covered for the last", "20 to 40 days"] },
  { n: "02", t: "Pick",     s: ["Youngest leaves,", "first harvest only"] },
  { n: "03", t: "Steam",    s: ["Within hours,", "to stop oxidation"] },
  { n: "04", t: "Dry",      s: ["Cooled, then", "dried flat"] },
  { n: "05", t: "Destem",   s: ["Stem and vein out.", "This is tencha"] },
  { n: "06", t: "Grind",    s: ["Granite, slowly.", "30 to 40g an hour"] },
];

const essays = [
  {
    title: "My Lifelong Career as a Reader and Writer",
    where: "Translingual, Issue 6, page 26",
    href: "https://ielp.ehe.osu.edu/files/2026/03/Translingual-Issue-6.pdf",
    note: "On reading as something inherited before it was chosen, and what it cost to keep.",
  },
  {
    title: "A Film Analysis: Grave of the Fireflies",
    where: "Translingual, Issue 2, April 2023",
    note: "How an antiwar film does its damage without a single scare, and why that lasts longer.",
  },
  {
    title: "Shades of Black",
    where: "Translingual, Issue 2, April 2023",
    note: "A remark about always wearing black, followed further than the person making it intended.",
  },
  {
    title: "Imprisonment in The Allegory of the Cave and The House of Asterion",
    where: "Unpublished",
    note: "Plato and Borges on the same question: whether a prisoner who cannot see the walls is still one.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="The Rough"
  description="Where the green and the stone on this site came from. Matcha as a morning ritual, and four essays. By Linh (Min) Le."
>
  <article class="rough">

    <header class="band g-ivory rough-head">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Beyond work</p>
        <h1>The Rough</h1>
        <p class="rough-lede">
          This site is green and its mark is a stone, and neither of those was chosen at a desk.
          Both come from things I do when nobody is paying me to.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="band plated g-leaf" style="--plate: var(--g-beige);">
      <div class="shell prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Matcha</p>
        <h2 class="words" data-words>Everything that decides whether it is good happened before I touched it</h2>

        <p>
          I make it every morning. There is a full set at home, bowl and whisk, and a corner of the
          kitchen that exists for nothing else. The twenty minutes it takes are the part of the day
          I am most reliably calm, and on the days I skip it I notice.
        </p>
        <p>
          What holds my attention is not the drink at the end. It is that almost every decision
          determining whether the drink is any good was made months earlier, by someone else, in a
          sequence that does not allow going backwards.
        </p>

        <figure class="fig">
          <div class="fig-frame">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 760 150" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" role="img"
                 aria-label="Six stages of matcha production, from shading in the field through to stone grinding.">
              {steps.map((st, i) => (
                <g class={st.t === "Grind" ? "st on" : "st"}>
                  <rect x={8 + i * 124} y="26" width="112" height="86" rx="7"/>
                  <text class="sn" x={20 + i * 124} y="44">{st.n}</text>
                  <text class="stt" x={20 + i * 124} y="63">{st.t}</text>
                  {st.s.map((ln, k) => (
                    <text class="sss" x={20 + i * 124} y={81 + k * 11}>{ln}</text>
                  ))}
                  {i < 5 && <path class="arw" d={`M${120 + i * 124} 69 l9 0 m-3.5 -3.5 l3.5 3.5 l-3.5 3.5`}/>}
                </g>
              ))}
              <text class="cap" x="8" y="136">Only after 05 is it tencha, which means tea for grinding. It is not matcha until 06.</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </figure>

        <p>
          The plants are covered for the last twenty to forty days before picking. Starved of light
          they push out chlorophyll and convert catechins into L-theanine, which is why the powder is
          that green and why the taste moves from bitter toward sweet. Only the youngest leaves of the
          first harvest are taken. They are steamed within hours to stop oxidation, then cooled and
          dried, then stripped of stem and vein until only leaf flesh is left.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then it goes between two granite stones turning slowly enough to produce thirty to forty
          grams in an hour. The slowness is the whole point. Grinding faster makes heat, and heat
          takes the aroma with it.
        </p>
        <p class="beat">By the time it reaches me, none of that is recoverable.</p>
        <p>
          What I control is the last four minutes. Water temperature, the ratio, how the whisk moves.
          Everything upstream has already set the ceiling, and no amount of care at my end raises it.
        </p>
        <p>
          I like work that behaves this way, where quality is decided early and quietly and the
          visible part at the end is small. It is also, if I am honest, part of why I distrust a
          number that arrives looking finished.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is the only caffeine that agrees with me, too. Coffee gives me a spike and then takes it
          back with interest. Matcha carries L-theanine alongside the caffeine and the lift is flatter
          and lasts, which suits a morning that starts with reading something carefully.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band plated g-cream" style="--plate: var(--g-ivory);">
      <div class="shell prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Writing</p>
        <h2 class="words" data-words>Four essays, three of them published</h2>
        <p>
          Before any of the analysis, this. Three of these appeared in Translingual, the journal of
          Ohio State's International English Language Programs. The fourth was never submitted
          anywhere and is here because I still like it.
        </p>

        <ol class="essays">
          {essays.map((e) => (
            <li class="essay">
              <h3 class="essay-title">
                {e.href ? <a href={e.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{e.title}</a> : e.title}
              </h3>
              <p class="essay-where figure">{e.where}</p>
              <p class="essay-note">{e.note}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .rough-head { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .rough-head h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -.02em;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-top: .3rem;
  }
  .rough-lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -.015em;
    margin: .3rem 0 1.3rem;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .prose p { margin-bottom: 1.05em; line-height: 1.62; }
  .prose .beat {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 60, "WONK" 1;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .fig { margin: 1.6rem 0 1.8rem; }
  .fig-frame {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: .8rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .fig-frame svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 34rem; height: auto; }
  .st rect { fill: none; stroke: var(--rule-strong); stroke-width: 1; }
  .st.on rect { fill: var(--accent-wash); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .sn  { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 8px; fill: var(--ink-faint); letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .stt { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--ink); }
  .st.on .stt { fill: var(--accent-deep); }
  .sss { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 7.5px; fill: var(--ink-soft); }
  .cap { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 8px; fill: var(--ink-faint); letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .arw { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }

  .essays { list-style: none; margin: 1.4rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .essay { padding: 1.1rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .essay:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  .essay-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 40;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .essay-title a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent-line); }
  .essay-title a:hover { color: var(--accent-deep); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .essay-where {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    letter-spacing: .05em;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    margin-top: .3rem;
  }
  .essay-note { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); margin-top: .45rem; line-height: 1.55; }
</style>
